---
import Layout from '../../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="SongCue Privacy Policy"
	description="Privacy Policy for SongCue, the Apple Music guessing game for friends"
	pubDate={new Date('September 5 2026')}
>
	<h2>Privacy Policy for SongCue</h2>
	<p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 5, 2026</p>

	<h3>Introduction</h3>
	<p>
		SongCue ("we", "our", or "us") is an iOS app and iMessage extension that turns Apple Music
		into a guessing game between friends. We are committed to protecting your privacy. This
		Privacy Policy explains how we handle information when you use SongCue.
	</p>

	<h3>Information We Collect</h3>
	<p>
		<strong>SongCue does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data.</strong> There are no
		servers and no analytics. We do not:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Collect your name, email address, or phone number</li>
		<li>Require you to create an account</li>
		<li>Track your location</li>
		<li>Access your contacts, photos, microphone, or camera</li>
		<li>Use analytics, crash reporting, or tracking SDKs</li>
		<li>Use third-party advertising networks</li>
		<li>Sell or share data with anyone</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Challenges and Profile Data</h3>
	<p>
		The challenges you create, the challenges friends send you, your scores, and your display
		name and colour are stored locally on your device in a shared container (an App Group) so
		that the SongCue app and its iMessage extension can both read them. This data never leaves
		your device except when you choose to share a challenge or a score with a friend. If you
		uninstall the app, this data is removed with it.
	</p>

	<h3>Apple Music</h3>
	<p>
		SongCue uses Apple's MusicKit to search the Apple Music catalog and play song snippets under
		your own Apple Music subscription. When you grant SongCue access to Apple Music, requests go
		directly from your device to Apple. We never see your Apple ID, your listening history, or
		your library. Apple's handling of this data is governed by
		<a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>.
	</p>

	<h3>Sharing over iMessage</h3>
	<p>
		When you send a challenge or a score, the data travels inside the iMessage message itself.
		It is delivered by Apple's Messages service to the people you choose, and we do not have a
		copy of it. Messages are protected according to Apple's iMessage policies. Anyone who
		receives a challenge can see its name, colour, the song list, the cue positions, and the
		display name you chose in SongCue.
	</p>

	<h3>Third-Party Services</h3>
	<p>
		Other than Apple Music and iMessage, both operated by Apple on your device, SongCue does not
		integrate with any third-party services.
	</p>

	<h3>Children's Privacy</h3>
	<p>
		SongCue does not collect personal information from anyone, including children under 13
		years of age.
	</p>

	<h3>App Store Information</h3>
	<p>
		When you download SongCue from the Apple App Store, Apple may collect information according
		to its own privacy policy. We do not receive personally identifiable information from Apple
		beyond aggregated, anonymous download and crash statistics that Apple provides to all
		developers.
	</p>

	<h3>Changes to This Policy</h3>
	<p>
		We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this
		page with an updated "Last Updated" date.
	</p>

	<h3>Contact Us</h3>
	<p>
		If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:
	</p>
	<p>
		<a href="mailto:evan+songcue@mightystrong.io">evan+songcue@mightystrong.io</a>
	</p>
</Layout>
